task_dir: /Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben

You need to add unit tests to fix identified coverage gaps. DO NOT modify implementation files — only test files.

Read each implementation file first to understand the exact logic, then add the tests.

## Gap 1: Binance empty params known-value signature

File: `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/binance.test.ts`

The existing test "handles empty params object" only checks URL format. Add a NEW test that verifies the actual computed signature value when params is `{}`:
```typescript
it("produces correct signature with empty params", () => {
  const { createHmac } = require("node:crypto");
  const credentials = { api_key: "key", secret: "secret" };
  const result = binanceExchange.sign(credentials, {
    method: "GET",
    path: "/api/v3/account",
    timestamp: "123",
    params: {},
  });
  const expected = createHmac("sha256", "secret").update("timestamp=123").digest("hex");
  expect(result.url).toContain(`signature=${expected}`);
});
```

Also add a meta test for referral_url and api_doc_url:
```typescript
it("has referral and api doc URLs", () => {
  expect(binanceExchange.referral_url).toBeDefined();
  expect(binanceExchange.api_doc_url).toBeDefined();
});
```

## Gap 2: Bybit body parameter is ignored

File: `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/bybit.test.ts`

Read the bybit.ts implementation to confirm body is not used in signing. Then add:
```typescript
it("produces same signature regardless of body parameter", () => {
  const credentials = { api_key: "k", secret: "s" };
  const base = { method: "POST" as const, path: "/v5/order/create", timestamp: "123" };
  const withBody = bybitExchange.sign(credentials, { ...base, body: '{"side":"Buy"}' });
  const withoutBody = bybitExchange.sign(credentials, { ...base });
  expect(withBody.headers["X-BAPI-SIGN"]).toBe(withoutBody.headers["X-BAPI-SIGN"]);
});
```

## Gap 3: Gate params participate in signature computation

File: `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/gate.test.ts`

Read gate.ts to understand how params/queryString is part of the prehash. Add:
```typescript
it("params affect the computed signature", () => {
  const credentials = { api_key: "k", secret: "s" };
  const base = { method: "GET" as const, path: "/api/v4/spot/accounts", timestamp: "123" };
  const withParams = gateExchange.sign(credentials, { ...base, params: { currency: "BTC" } });
  const withoutParams = gateExchange.sign(credentials, { ...base });
  expect(withParams.headers["SIGN"]).not.toBe(withoutParams.headers["SIGN"]);
});
```

## Gap 4: Lighter undefined body = empty body

File: `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/lighter.test.ts`

Read lighter.ts to confirm `body ?? ""` is used. Add:
```typescript
it("undefined body produces same signature as empty string body", () => {
  const credentials = { api_key: "k", secret: "s" };
  const base = { method: "GET" as const, path: "/api/v1/account", timestamp: "123" };
  const undefinedBody = lighterExchange.sign(credentials, { ...base });
  const emptyBody = lighterExchange.sign(credentials, { ...base, body: "" });
  expect(undefinedBody.headers["X-LIGHTER-SIGN"]).toBe(emptyBody.headers["X-LIGHTER-SIGN"]);
});
```

## Gap 5: test-connection passes correct headers from sign() to fetch()

File: `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/test-connection.test.ts`

Add a test that verifies the fetch call includes the headers produced by sign(). Pick OKX as example:
```typescript
it("passes signed headers to fetch (okx)", async () => {
  const mockFetch = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, status: 200, text: async () => '{"code":"0"}' });
  vi.stubGlobal("fetch", mockFetch);
  await okxExchange.testConnection({ api_key: "mykey", secret: "mysecret", passphrase: "mypass" });
  const [, opts] = mockFetch.mock.calls[0];
  expect(opts.headers["OK-ACCESS-KEY"]).toBe("mykey");
  expect(opts.headers["OK-ACCESS-PASSPHRASE"]).toBe("mypass");
  expect(opts.headers["OK-ACCESS-SIGN"]).toBeDefined();
  expect(opts.headers["OK-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP"]).toBeDefined();
});
```

After adding ALL tests, run:
```
npx vitest run packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/binance.test.ts packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/bybit.test.ts packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/gate.test.ts packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/lighter.test.ts packages/core/src/account/ops/exchanges/test-connection.test.ts
```

Verify all tests pass.

